Functional Interface

the interface who contains only one abstract method but can have multiple
defulet nad static method is called functional interface.

Runnable-------------> run()
callable-------------> call()
Comparable-----------> compareTo()
comparator-----------> compare()

//Steps to make any Function lambda expression

// 1)  Remove modifier
// 2) remove retuen type
// 3) remove method name
// 4) place arrow



public void sayHello(){
System.out.print("i am ankit");
}

()->{
System.out.print("i am ankit");
};

public int add(int a,int b){
System.out.print(a+b);
}


(int a,int b)->{
System.out.print(a+b);
}

(a,b)->System.out.print(a+b);




private int getStringLength(String str){
return str.lenth();
}


(String str)->{
return str.lenth();
}

(String str)-> return str.lenth();
